HanaWorlds Canvas 0.13.2 component candidate.

Owner-authored source is MIT; see LICENSE and LICENSE_AUDIT.md. The 0.1.0
AGPL-3.0-only source remains available at public revision
d27be3f51e6733ab4f720700bb86145e9a578a5d. All source and test changes in
that baseline are authored by yzsnstotz; no third-party source is vendored.

Runtime dependencies are separate packages. canonicalize 5.1.0 is Apache-2.0;
icu 2.3.1 is Unicode-3.0. Their notices and license texts remain with the
separately installed npm packages. WorldEdit (AGPL-3.0) and the Luanti Adapter
are separate origins and are not bundled or relicensed by Canvas.

hanaworlds-contracts (MIT, HanaWorlds-owned) is a separately installed
dependency from https://github.com/yzsnstotz/hanaworlds-contracts
(exact public git tag v2.2.1); no Contracts bytes are copied into this repository.

Canvas display bundle includes Zod 4.6.5 (MIT) from the official DSH runtime,
https://github.com/colinhacks/zod, for the public Remote schemas. Host peers:
@deepseek-ai/cordis 4.0.4 and @deepseek-ai/dsh-typert-protocol 0.2.0-rc.2 (MIT),
from the official deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness runtime. React 18.3.1 (MIT),
https://github.com/facebook/react, is a development/render dependency; the
browser uses DSH's shared React seed. esbuild 0.25.10 (MIT),
https://github.com/evanw/esbuild, builds the client bundle and is not a runtime.

ReactDOM 18.3.1 (MIT) renders isolated tests only; the independent fixture pages
are archived outside the shipped package. DSH registry/gateway/util-crypto
0.2.0-rc.2 (MIT) are development dependencies for the official remote test path.
